Description: graphical analyser and benchmark for USB storage devices
 USB Speed Tester is a PyQt6 desktop application that runs the usual Linux
 USB diagnostic tools and explains their output in plain language. It reports
 the negotiated link speed of the bus (5000M for USB 3.x, 480M for USB 2.0),
 cached and physical read speed with hdparm, real write speed with dd,
 sequential and 4K random throughput and IOPS with fio, and SMART health data
 with smartctl whenever the USB bridge forwards it.
 .
 Results are shown in a technical log with the raw command output next to a
 user analysis that says what the numbers mean in practice, for example
 whether a slow pendrive is limited by the port or by the flash chip itself.
 .
 An illustrated tutorial explains how to recognise a real USB 3.x SuperSpeed
 port by the SS marking printed a few millimetres from the connector. The
 interface, the tutorial and the About box are available in English and
 Spanish.
